    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "literal.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only is_word_char. The body is one expression: ch == '\\'' || ch == '\\u{2019}' || char_matches(ch, class_re(r\"\\A\\w\\z\", 0)). Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch find, empty_spans, find_exact, find_folded, is_whole_word, or is_boundary. The existing tests an_apostrophe_is_inside_a_word and an_empty_whole_word_finds_nothing stay green. Do not rewrite their assertions. The test a_curly_apostrophe_is_inside_a_word uses Rope::from_str of don, U+2019, and t. is_whole_word of 0 and 3 is false. is_whole_word of 0 and 5 is true. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
